                'description_en' => 'Luis Raymund "L-Ray" Villafuerte Jr. (born June 3, 1968) served as governor of Camarines Sur for three consecutive terms from 2004 to 2013. During his tenure, Camarines Sur was recognized for tourism and development projects: the CamSur Watersports Complex (CWC), the promotion of Caramoan as a tourism destination, the El Verde tree-planting movement, and the construction of an IT park managed by the local government. It was also reported that the economic status of the province rose during this period. After his first three terms, he served as Representative of the Second District of Camarines Sur, and in 2025 was re-elected as governor — his fourth term overall.',
